From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:29:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 27/77] fphttpserver: call OnAllowConnect again

Since the server socket's OnConnectSocketQuery was routed through
DoOnAllowConnect (connection limit, 503), the user's OnAllowConnect was
stored but never called. Servers that refuse connections or stop their
accept loop from it (lantaarn's viewer server stops while connections keep
coming) no longer could. Call it after the connection-limit check, with
the arguments the 3.2 wiring (FServer.OnConnectQuery) passed.
---
 packages/fcl-web/src/base/fphttpserver.pp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/packages/fcl-web/src/base/fphttpserver.pp b/packages/fcl-web/src/base/fphttpserver.pp
index 07f1424e..a2a85b11 100644
--- a/packages/fcl-web/src/base/fphttpserver.pp
+++ b/packages/fcl-web/src/base/fphttpserver.pp
@@ -1298,7 +1298,13 @@ begin
     allow:=False;
     end
   else
+    begin
     Allow:=True;
+    { The user's OnAllowConnect (wired directly to the socket server's
+      OnConnectQuery up to 3.2) still decides on the connection }
+    if Assigned(FOnAllowConnect) then
+      FOnAllowConnect(Sender,ASocket.FD,Allow);
+    end;
 end;
 
 procedure TFPCustomHttpServer.DoAcceptIdle(Sender: TObject);
